// A rover patrolling the 4-node waypoint map (Stringer, Figures 7.1, 7.2 and 7.8).
// The route starting and ending at waypoint a visits b, d, c and b (Equation 7.1).
// If an action stops doing what its description says the rover detects this, learns
// a new description of the action and patches its route.

GWENDOLEN

:name: rover

:Initial Beliefs:

:Capabilities:
{at(a)} move(a,b) {at(b), ~at(a)}
{at(b)} move(b,a) {at(a), ~at(b)}
{at(a)} move(a,c) {at(c), ~at(a)}
{at(c)} move(c,a) {at(a), ~at(c)}
{at(b)} move(b,d) {at(d), ~at(b)}
{at(d)} move(d,b) {at(b), ~at(d)}
{at(c)} move(c,d) {at(d), ~at(c)}
{at(d)} move(d,c) {at(c), ~at(d)}
{at(a)} move(a,d) {at(d), ~at(a)}
{at(d)} move(d,a) {at(a), ~at(d)}
{at(b)} move(b,c) {at(c), ~at(b)}
{at(c)} move(c,b) {at(b), ~at(c)}

:Initial Goals:
patrol [perform]

:Plans:
+!patrol [perform] : {True} <- +!route [perform], +!route [perform], print(patrolled);

+!route [perform] : {B at(a)} <- move(a,b), move(b,d), move(d,c), move(c,b), move(b,a);
